  "emphasis": {
    "primary": "Damage (Explosion area attacks)",
    "secondary": "Afterburn and Increase Damage Taken (Charge 4 Explosion pressure)",
    "tertiary": "Decrease Damage Taken and Increase Damage Given (Blast Shield / charge buffs)",
    "rationale": "Three of the eight supported rows are Explosion damage on 60 AP area attacks (Kinetic Nova 50, Inferno Cataclysm 40, Howitzer Crash 40 at jutsu level 25), so burst is the declared role. Charge 4 Explosion carries three supported rows on one 40 AP single-target cast (self Increase Damage Given 35%, enemy Increase Damage Taken 35%, Afterburn 35%, two rounds each), which makes it the pressure hub; Howitzer Crash adds a second Increase Damage Given row as a ground circle. Blast Shield's single Decrease Damage Taken row (35%, self and allies in its radius) is the only defensive row. There are no heal, lifesteal, reflect or Decrease Damage Given rows, so no sustain or suppression route is invented."
  },
